# Extended Error Help: {{ .errorCode }}

## What happened?
Hydra needs a context path before it can inspect apps, values, or manifests.
Neither the `--hydra-context` flag nor the `{{ .ENV }}` environment variable was set.

## Why Hydra stops here
Most local commands need to know which Hydra repository context they should read from.
Without that path, Hydra cannot resolve clusters or applications safely.

## Resolution
Set one of these before retrying:

```bash
export {{ .ENV }}=/path/to/context
```

or:

```bash
hydra local apps --hydra-context /path/to/context
```

## Next step
Create or choose the target context directory first, then point Hydra at it.
